H2: Known Faults - Volvo XC60
P: Each fault below carries the years the source gives for it.
H3: Diesel EGR and DPF (2008-2017)
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2017 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says that on the 2008-2017 XC60 the Euro 6 diesels, especially the D4, suffer problems with the water-cooled exhaust gas recirculation (EGR) system, which can become clogged with soot. Parkers adds that with higher mileages and neglect, oil leaks may indicate imminent turbo failure, and problems with the DPF and EGR valve are common as the cars get older.
H3: Diesel DPF and Turbo (2017 on)
P: MONITOR ú 2017 on ú Get a quote
P: What Car? reports that diesel models were particularly prone to problems with the Diesel Particulate Filter (DPF) and turbochargers, leading to costly repairs. Autocar says reduced engine performance in a diesel could point to a clogged diesel particulate filter, which is often caused by a busted oxygen sensor.
H3: Oil Consumption on Pre-2016 2.0 Diesels
P: MONITOR ú 2008-2017 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says high oil consumption is a problem with pre-2016 models (engine number prior to 1501327) that can require new pistons and rings to rectify. The RAC says pre-2016 models can suffer high oil consumption that can only be rectified expensively, while EGR valves are prone to issues.
H3: Plug-in Hybrid Rear Drive (ERAD)
P: HIGH ú 2017 on ú Get a quote
P: On plug-in hybrid (PHEV) versions, What Car? says to pay particular attention to the Electric Rear Axle Drive (ERAD). Listen for unusual whining, howling, grinding or knocking noises from the rear when driving in electric mode, particularly if the noise increases with road speed. Hesitation when the electric motor engages, a lack of electric drive or a hybrid-system warning can also indicate a problem. What Car? puts a complete ERAD replacement at around œ9000-œ10,000, with specialist repairs typically costing around œ3000-œ4000. Autocar says the T8 PHEV's supercharger seals can fail and hamper performance.
H3: Hybrid Battery and Charging
P: MONITOR ú 2017 on ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says hybrid owners mentioned battery and charging system issues, with some experiencing reduced electric range over time. Volvo UK's warranty page covers the High Voltage Battery for eight years or 100,000 miles, whichever comes first, from the date the vehicle is delivered to its first owner. The cover applies if the battery's State-of-Health (SoH) drops below 70% of its original capacity.
H3: Petrol Engines Burning Oil
P: MONITOR ú 2017-2024 ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says that on the 2017-2024 XC60 petrol cars can burn oil. Check the oil level when you view a car and ask whether it has needed top-ups.
H3: Electrical Faults and Touchscreen
P: CHECK ú 2014 on ú Get a quote
P: The RAC says early cars could suffer expensive electrical gremlins, so check everything works on a test drive. For the 2017-2024 car, Autocar says electrical issues can knock out various different functions like the electric handbrake, which may turn on by itself. It also says to check the touchscreen is not suffering from any latency issues or software gremlins.
H3: Geartronic Automatic
P: MINOR ú 2008-2017 ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says the Volvo Geartronic transmission has a relatively poor reputation among used buyers, but it is no better or worse than other automatic cars of the era.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several XC60 recalls, including these.
LI: Vehicles may have the Supplementary Restraint System (SRS) control unit incorrectly tightened to the car body.
LI: Vehicles may have incorrectly tightened front wiper arm securing nuts.
LI: Potential breakage/fatigue of a flexible steel cable supporting the front seatbelt anchor point.
LI: The Automatic Emergency Brake System a function of the IntelliSafe system may not always engage increasing the risk of a collision.
LI: Possible loss of power whilst driving.
P: To see whether a particular car has an open recall, enter its registration in our recall check .
