H2: Known Faults - Volvo V60
P: The faults below come from reviews of the 2010-2018 V60 and the 2018 on car.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: MONITOR ú 2010-2018 early diesels ú Garage quote needed
P: What Car? says early diesel-engined cars could have problems with diesel particulate filters clogging, but this was often remedied with a good, long drive. If a diesel you are viewing has a warning light showing, ask the seller what has been done about it.
H3: EGR Valve on D4 Diesels
P: CHECK ú 2010-2018 D4 diesels ú Garage quote needed
P: What Car? says problems were reported with the EGRs of certain D4-engined cars, leading to the check engine light coming on and the car occasionally going into limp home mode. The review does not say which D4 cars or which years were hit. Ask whether the engine light has ever come on, and what was done.
H3: Low-Rev Clunks
P: MINOR ú 2010-2018 diesels ú Garage quote needed
P: What Car? says clunks have been reported at low revs in the diesels, although this hasn't necessarily led to the car breaking down. Listen for them at low speed on a test drive.
H3: Gear Shifts
P: CHECK ú 2014-2018 ú Garage quote needed
P: In its review of the 2014-2018 car, the RAC says some owners have reported problems with jerky or jumping gear shifting. Drive the car through the gears, and from a stop, before you agree a price.
H3: Warning Lights and Electronics
P: MONITOR ú 2018 on ú Garage quote needed
P: What Car? says the 2018 on V60 seems to have a mixed reliability record. It gives the car a reliability rating of 85.5% and calls that disappointing. It adds that others reported recurring problems, including faulty warning lights, electronic glitches and drivetrain malfunctions. In its advice page, What Car? says reliability can be an issue. Auto Express says reliability can be disappointing.
H3: Reliability Results
P: What Car? says the 2010-2018 generation did rather well in its most recent reliability survey, securing a third place finish in the executive car class that consisted of 22 models. It also says that, on the whole, the V60 has a good reputation for reliability. The RAC says reliability shouldn't be an issue on the 2010-2013 car.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several V60 recalls, including these.
LI: For affected vehicles there is a potential defect in the torsion bar within the front seatbelt system.
LI: The rod connecting the brake pedal to the brake booster may not have been assembled correctly.
LI: The Engine Control Module (ECM) may prevent the combustion engine from starting.
LI: There may be an insufficient or missing welding connection in the Hydraulic Unit of the Brake System.
LI: Pressure in the fuel tank could cause the fuel level sender to indicate fuel in the tank when it could be empty.
P: Not every car is affected, so check the one you are buying with our recall check .
