H2: Known Faults - Volvo V90
H3: What Car? Reliability Survey
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2025 cars ú Get a quote
P: In its reliability review of the used 2016-2025 V90, What Car? says its data suggests the car is below average for reliability. It puts the reliability score at 76.7%.
P: Parkers, in its buying guide to the 2016-2025 V90, says not to expect Volvo's granite-like reputation for reliability, as there are a few concerns it goes into in more detail.
P: Auto Express says neither the S90 nor the V90 has made it into its Driver Power new or used car surveys, because they do not sell in big enough numbers.
H3: Bodywork, Electrical and Engine Reports
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2025 cars ú Get a quote
P: In the What Car? survey, bodywork drew the most complaints, with 8.5% of V90 owners seeing problems. Electrical faults and engine issues were cited as well, with 6.8% of owners (each) experiencing problems.
P: What Car? adds that a few owners reported only minor electronic and software glitches, which were typically resolved quickly by dealers.
H3: Infotainment System
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2025 cars ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says most of the grumbles it has come across with V90s relate to the infotainment system and the plethora of gremlins within it. It says patchy connections, freezing and resets are all commonplace.
H3: Diesel Particulate Filter
P: MONITOR ú Diesels ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says diesel V90s all have a diesel particulate filter (DPF) that can clog with time, especially if the car is used on lots of shorter trips.
H3: Brake and Disc Wear
P: MONITOR ú 2016-2025 cars ú Get a quote
P: Parkers says the V90 is a heavy car and is known to eat through brakes quickly. It says to watch out for a squeaking noise or juddering sensation under braking, because it can point to warped discs or worn pads.
H3: Touchscreen, Build Quality and Cruise Control, Owners' Reports
P: CHECK ú Owners' reports ú Get a quote
P: One Parkers owner of a D4 Inscription Geartronic wrote that the touchscreen system is distracting and dangerous, because it controls everything including the climate control. They also wrote that build quality is well below traditional Volvo standards.
P: One Parkers owner of a D5 PowerPulse Inscription AWD Geartronic wrote that the cruise control starts braking too early when catching up with other cars doing slower speeds.
P: To see whether a DVSA safety recall is open on a V90 you are weighing up, type its registration into our recall check . Engines, power outputs and trims for each version are on the Volvo V90 parts page .
H2: Breakdown cover
P: If a fault stops the car on the road, breakdown cover sends help to you. Compare two UK providers and check what each policy includes.
P: We earn a commission if you buy cover through these links, at no cost to you ( how we're paid ).
H2: Volvo V90 MOT results in 2025
P: There were 16,684 MOT tests of the Volvo V90 in 2025. 15.9% failed first time, against 27.7% for all cars. Older cars fail more often, so the fairer comparison is by age:
H3: What they failed on
LI: Tyres : 6.2% of tests (all cars 6.2%)
LI: Brakes : 3.4% of tests (all cars 6.2%). Brake pad prices , brake disc prices
LI: Suspension : 2.4% of tests (all cars 9.0%). Shock absorber prices
LI: Lamps, reflectors and electrical equipment : 2.2% of tests (all cars 10.6%). Headlight bulb prices by type
LI: Body, chassis, structure : 2.2% of tests (all cars 3.3%)
P: Initial MOT tests in Great Britain, 2025, from DVSA's anonymised MOT data; fail rate as DVSA calculates it (fails plus faults fixed during the test). Results cover every car recorded under the model name, so the older age bands can include earlier generations of it. Contains public sector information licensed under the Open Government Licence v3.0. MOT pass rates for every model and how they're worked out .
