H2: Frequently asked questions
P: What Car? says its data suggests the V90 is below average for reliability, with a reliability score of 76.7%. Parkers says not to expect Volvo&#39;s granite-like reputation for reliability with a used V90, because there are a few concerns.
P: In the What Car? owner survey, bodywork drew reports from 8.5% of V90 owners, while electrical faults and engine issues were each cited by 6.8%. Parkers says most of the grumbles it has come across relate to the infotainment system.
P: Parkers says diesel V90s all have a diesel particulate filter (DPF) that can clog with time, especially if the car is used on lots of shorter trips.
P: Auto Express says neither the S90 nor the V90 has made it into its Driver Power new or used car surveys, because they do not sell in big enough numbers.
