H2: Known Faults - Volvo S60
H3: Exhaust System on Diesels
P: MONITOR ú 2010-2018 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says problems have been reported with the exhaust system on some diesels in the 2010-2018 S60.
H3: Heated Rear Screen
P: MINOR ú 2010-2018 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? reports failures of the heated rear screen on the 2010-2018 S60.
H3: Adaptive Cruise Control Radar
P: MONITOR ú 2010-2018 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? reports failures of the radar system, which helps cruise control to maintain a set distance from the car in front. It also says S60s that are equipped with adaptive cruise control can suffer from problems with it.
H3: Power Steering Belt and Return Line
P: MONITOR ú 2010-2018 ú Get a quote
P: What Car? says the auxiliary drive belt that powers the power steering pump can fail and affect the power steering system. It also says a power steering return line can leak fluid.
H3: Front Tyre Wear
P: CHECK ú 2000-2009 ú Get a quote
P: For the first-generation S60, What Car? says front tyre wear is a problem common to all S60s because the powerful engines drive the front wheels. It says it is easy to get through a set in 12,000 miles, so allow for this in your budget.
H3: Four-Wheel-Drive System on the S60 R
P: CHECK ú 2003 on ú Get a quote
P: Autocar says a frequent fault in the S60 R, which it dates from 2003, is with the four-wheel drive system. The transfer case, or the splined sleeve for the propshaft that drives the rear wheels, can fail. As a result, Autocar says, a lot of four-wheel-drive S60 Rs end up being front-wheel drive only.
H3: Reliability Survey Results
P: For the 2010-2018 car, What Car? says Volvo as a brand finished in 11th place out of 31 manufacturers in its latest reliability survey. Carbuyer says Volvo as a brand was rated 13th out of 26 carmakers on the UK market for overall satisfaction, and that the S60 does not feature in its 2018 Driver Power customer satisfaction survey.
P: For the 2018-2023 car, What Car? says the S60 finished in ninth place out of 25 cars in the executive car class in its most recent reliability survey, and that Volvo as a manufacturer ranked 15th out of 32 brands. In 2022 Carbuyer said the S60 itself had not featured in the results in recent years, with the brand coming ninth out of 29 manufacturers in its 2021 Driver Power owner satisfaction survey. Carbuyer sums the car up as having impressive safety technology but reliability that remains to be proven.
H3: DVSA Safety Recalls
P: DVSA's recall data lists several S60 recalls, including these.
LI: The passenger air bag may not have been correctly secured.
LI: It is possible that due to a software issue fuel may not be pumped from one side (passive side) of the fuel tank to the other side (active side).
LI: Vehicles may have an incorrectly manufactured fuel supply line which could lead to fuel leakage.
LI: It is possible that the driver's and passenger's front powered seats may not be fitted with the front stop lug.
LI: On certain five cylinder engines it is possible that the high pressure fuel pipes may not have been correctly installed and may leak.
LI: When driving at low speeds a fault within the software calibration of the engine and transmission control modules may lead to a drop in the engine idle speed when braking or releasing the accelerator.
P: Enter a registration in our recall check to see whether a car has an open recall.
